14:T46d,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","headline":"Pakistan Prayer Times Master Guide: Karachi, Lahore, and Peshawar Daily Waqt Schedules, Banuri Town Standards, and Mosque Timetables","description":"Complete guide to namaz timing in Karachi, Lahore, and Peshawar. Details on Banuri Town standards, Hanafi Asr calculations, and daily mosque timetables.","image":["https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1564769625905-50e93615e769?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80"],"datePublished":"2026-10-12T10:15:00Z","dateModified":"2026-10-12T10:15:00Z","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Mufti Muhammad Arshad & Editorial Team","url":"https://namazeshariq.com/about"},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Namaz-e-Shariq","url":"https://namazeshariq.com","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://namazeshariq.com/web-app-manifest-512x512.png"}},"mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://namazeshariq.com/blog/pakistan-prayer-times-master-guide-karachi-lahore-peshawar"},"keywords":"namaz timing karachi, namaz time karachi, namaz timing lahore, namaz timing peshawar, isha namaz time pak, pakistan prayer timetable"}15:T664,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the official prayer calculation authority for Karachi and Pakistan?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The primary reference throughout Pakistan is the Department of Falakiyyat (Astronomy) at Jamia Uloom-ul-Islamia Banuri Town, Karachi, and the Central Ruet-e-Hilal Committee. They mandate the 18° twilight angle for both Subh Sadiq (Fajr) and Shafaq Abyad (Isha)."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why does Karachi have a different prayer schedule from Lahore?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Karachi is situated at latitude 24.86°N and longitude 67.00°E on the Arabian Sea coast, while Lahore is situated further north and east at latitude 31.52°N and longitude 74.35°E. Because Lahore is about 7.35 degrees east of Karachi, sunrise, noon, and sunset occur roughly 29 to 30 minutes earlier in Lahore."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"When does Sehri end in Karachi and Lahore?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Sehri time officially ends at the exact onset of Subh Sadiq (Fajr start time). As a precaution (Ihtiyat), scholars recommend concluding food and drink 5 minutes prior to the calculated Subh Sadiq."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do Ramadan sirens operate across Pakistani cities?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In Karachi, Lahore, Peshawar, and other major districts, historical and civic sirens sound at the exact entry of Maghrib for Iftar, and 5 to 10 minutes prior to Subh Sadiq as an alert for Sehri conclusion, synchronized with the central observatory timetables."}}]}a:["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-950 min-h-screen py-10 transition-colors duration-200","children":[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$14"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://namazeshariq.com\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Articles\",\"item\":\"https://namazeshariq.com/blog\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"Pakistan Prayer Times Master Guide: Karachi, Lahore, and Peshawar Daily Waqt Schedules, Banuri Town Standards, and Mosque Timetables\",\"item\":\"https://namazeshariq.com/blog/pakistan-prayer-times-master-guide-karachi-lahore-peshawar\"}]}"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$15"}}],"$L16"]}]
