21:["$","$L26",null,{"items":[{"question":"What is the official prayer calculation authority for Karachi and Pakistan?","answer":"The primary reference throughout Pakistan is the Department of Falakiyyat (Astronomy) at Jamia Uloom-ul-Islamia Banuri Town, Karachi, and the Central Ruet-e-Hilal Committee. They mandate the 18° twilight angle for both Subh Sadiq (Fajr) and Shafaq Abyad (Isha)."},{"question":"Why does Karachi have a different prayer schedule from Lahore?","answer":"Karachi is situated at latitude 24.86°N and longitude 67.00°E on the Arabian Sea coast, while Lahore is situated further north and east at latitude 31.52°N and longitude 74.35°E. Because Lahore is about 7.35 degrees east of Karachi, sunrise, noon, and sunset occur roughly 29 to 30 minutes earlier in Lahore."},{"question":"When does Sehri end in Karachi and Lahore?","answer":"Sehri time officially ends at the exact onset of Subh Sadiq (Fajr start time). As a precaution (Ihtiyat), scholars recommend concluding food and drink 5 minutes prior to the calculated Subh Sadiq."},{"question":"How do Ramadan sirens operate across Pakistani cities?","answer":"In Karachi, Lahore, Peshawar, and other major districts, historical and civic sirens sound at the exact entry of Maghrib for Iftar, and 5 to 10 minutes prior to Subh Sadiq as an alert for Sehri conclusion, synchronized with the central observatory timetables."}],"title":"Key Questions & Rulings Answered"}]
